<title>FRANCE: Accor 1996 net attrib profit 1.06 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Accor 1996 net attrib profit 1.06 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   1,058  vs	   923</p>
<p>    Net profit per share (francs)	  34.20  up 5.9 pct</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)			 20  unchanged</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)		     30  unchanged</p>
<p>    Operating				    2,576  vs	   2,919</p>
<p>    Financial loss			     1,260  vs	   1,640</p>
<p>    Turnover				    28,305  vs	  31,012</p>
<p>NOTE - Accor gave its results in a statement. It said it had seen a good start in the first quarter in Europe, with the exception of Europe. It is making an offer to buy out shareholders in Sphere International on a basis of one Accor share for every seven Sphere shares. Accor currently holds 77 percent of Sphere, which operates the Formule 1, Etap Hotel and Ibis chains. The merger will be positive for earnings by more than two francs per share.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
